# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD points at
# entrypoint.ps1, which is PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * Tomcat (catalina.bat) is launched in the BACKGROUND via Start-Process, so
#     the JVM is a detached child, NOT PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep -Seconds 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: Tomcat is ALREADY RUNNING with the vulnerable
# Struts app deployed, so removing the WAR and RESTARTING Tomcat (safe now - it
# is not PID 1) undeploys the in-memory OGNL surface. Restarting never kills the
# container.
